  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="FR">Output 1.2. Increased institutional capacity of workers&apos; organizations</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="FR">Timor-Leste Trade Union Confederation (KSTL) improved their services to members by developing and strengthening delegate structure and leadership at workplace level and  developing a strategy plan through participatory training.   

Increased capacities, commitment and engagement of Timor-Leste Trade Union Confederation and its delegate structures of the Unions improved services to members.
 The ILO conducted Leadership Training of Trainers for 30 union leaders of Timor-Leste Trade Union Confederation (KSTL) on 14-18 June 2021. Based on the TOT, with financial support from the ILO, KSTL will replicate the training for 130 union leader from 12 municipalities. The ILO also provided technical assistance and financial support for KSTL to conduct delegate development training for KSTL members in 12 municipalities to develop and strengthening delegate structure and leadership in their workplace. 
This training program is part of capacity building for trade union leaders and delegate and also part of organization development to improve the capacity of the leaders from workplaces level up to national level related to trade union administration and management financial.  This training program also will provide opportunity for participant to improve their knowledge and skills on trade union leadership, negotiation and organizing strategy.</narrative>
   </description>
